      "q": "10. State the causes of risks involved in business?\nBusiness risks can arise from various internal and external factors. Here are some of the main causes:\nInternal Causes: These stem from decisions or shortcomings within the business itself, such as:\nPoor management choices\nInefficient operations\nLack of innovation\nFinancial mismanagement\nExternal Causes: These are beyond the direct control of the business and can be more difficult to predict, such as:\nEconomic downturns\nChanges in government regulations\nFluctuations in the price of raw materials\nShifts in consumer preferences\nTechnological advancements by competitors\nNatural disasters or unexpected events\nLong Answers Questions",
